When I had my last ascension, which was also my first, I was very lucky. 
  I found a wand of wishing on dungeon level 6, and everything went 
pretty  smoothly after that. So this time, I decided to make things a 
little harder for myself. And I succeeded!

Silly started the way I think a lot of tourists start: as a distraction, 
a joke, not expecting him or her to live very long. I wanted to see how 
far I could get with these conducts (wishless, genoless, polypileless), 
not expecting to make it to the end.

The game started out pretty normal. I kept my pet near, descended as 
soon as I had mapped the entire level, and stole and price-id'ed from 
shops. There were a *lot* of shops in this game, in contrast to my last one.

Around dungeon level 8 (I always go for Sokoban first) I had a few close 
calls, where I had to dig down to escape a centaur, and pray for food. I 
also wasn't strong enough to wear the armor I wanted. Since this was 
from poison related strength drain, a unicorn horn from Sokoban fixed this.

Sokoban gave me the amulet, and with an AC of -1, I headed to the mines, 
still with my (now large) dog, Brutus. In minetown, I found a magic lamp 
(I would later find two more). Brutus killed the watch captain and the 
rest of the guards, and I took the saber. I also found Snickersnee lying 
in a shop! Even though I was neutral, I had Brutus steal it, and started 
two-weaponing it with the saber, something I did for the rest of the game.

On dungeon level 10 in the main dungeon, I found a bag of holding, which 
made things much easier for me, since I like to pick everything up 
anyway, and since I was going wishless, I had to carry around a lot of 
armor to buc-id it and find the highly enchanted ones.

Around dungeon level 19, it dawned on me that I might be too deep in the 
dungeon when an ettin and a mind flayer almost got me. So I went back 
up, bought some protection from the minetown priest (only the guaranteed 
priests were in this game) but sadly got Brutus killed on the way.

I found another BoH, set up a stash near an altar I converted, and went 
to the quest. Earlier I picked up teleportitis from a tengu, which had 
already made me steal from a shop. On the quest this happened again, and 
I killed the shopkeeper (it was an accident), which made me lose 
telepathy (and made me a murderer). The Master of Thieves was no 
problem. I put him asleep, and bashed him to death.

Until now, I didn't have magic resistance, so the PYEC was very welcome. 
It is really a great artifact; the charging is very powerful. And the 
telepathy was also welcome, since it took a while to find another 
floating eye.

I had also found a ring of levitation, so I went to see Medusa, which 
was fun, with a titan, a demi-lich and a master mind flayer. Then the 
castle, with the same titan (it had dug down), a demi-lich, two master 
liches and three rust monsters. The liches got my towel cursed while I 
was wearing it. Luckily I had picked up full range telepathy again.

The castle had speed boots, which gave me another part of my kit. I now 
had reflection (amulet), magic resistance (PYEC), speed boots, t-shirt, 
dwarvish mithril, cloak of protection, hard hat, and gloves of 
dexterity. I also had a unicorn horn, rings of conflict and levitation, 
some assorted wands and scrolls, and Snickersnee and the saber. I didn't 
think it was enough for Gehennom, so I started sacrificing.

The Lady gave me Vorpal Blade, Werebane, Trollsbane and Giantsmasher. So 
I kept Snickersnee, wrote some enchant armor scrolls (I found a magic 
marker, but almost no ?oEA), and used the enchant weapon scrolls I'd 
found. I also made some holy water, and descended down into Gehennom anyway.

I killed Asmodeus, Juiblex, Baalzebub and Orcus. By now, my teleportitis 
was getting annoying. I had just found a cursed (said the altar on 
Orcus' level) scroll of genocide, so I called in some tengu, which did 
what they were supposed to, and gave me teleport control.

I went down further, marked the vibrating sphere, killed Vlad and got 
his candelabrum, and went back up. And in the Valley of the Dead, it 
happened: I had locked a incubus there, and while unlocking the door, 
wanted to press (a)pply, <slot of the key>, (y)es. But I mistyped, and 
in the slot I chose to apply, there was a wand of cancellation! All 
enchantments gone, blessings, all gone. My AC went from -28 to -8, my 
weapons went from +3 and +5 to +0. Why does the game ask for 
confirmation for unlocking a door anyway? It's completely unnessecary.

I now searched the entire dungeons for forgotten scrolls of enchant 
armor and weapon. I went to Sokoban, the Quest and the mines again, and 
eventually found one of each. Then I wrote two more enchant armor 
scrolls. I also reverse genocided gray dragons for a backup source of 
magic resistance. After this and some alchemy, I had an AC of -25 and 
about 300 hp, and felt I could make the final run.

When I stood in from of Rodney's door, I found that I had forgotten to 
fireproof my cloak. I didn't have enough marker charges to write enchant 
armor, so I wrote destroy armor instead, which is why I had a burnt 
fireproof cloak on.

In Moloch's Sanctum, three liches (arch and two master) took me some 
time, but after a cockatrice left a corpse, the rest was easy. I stoned 
the high priest, knocked open the statue, and found what I was looking 
for. On the way up, the mysterious force was really annoying. I got 
pulled back 18 times!

In the Valley of the Dead, something funny happened. The WoY appeared, 
and I zapped him with a /oD. But the wand also hit the priest there. 
Moloch was mad at me, and sent in some lightning:

Moloch roars: "Thou dost profane my shire!" The bolt of lightning hits 
the priest of Moloch. The bolt of lightning hits you! But it reflects 
from your medallion! The bolt of lightning hits the priest of Moloch. 
You kill the priest of Moloch! You murderer!

But I didn't lose telepathy (?). At my stash I did some last 
preparations. Here, I found out that my ring I had marked "slow 
digestion" after dropping it in a sink and getting it back, was actually 
searching! I thought you only got SD back... stupid, since I had 
intrinsic searching since experience level 10, and had been wearing the 
ring almost the entire game.

I had only two scrolls of gold detection, but I had recharged a crystal 
ball for the occasion. On the way up I found another scroll of gold 
detection, so I thought I was set. Earth was uneventful, fire was quick, 
air was as well (I healed up once inside a vortex), and on water, I 
finally got out the crystal ball. I applied it, and it exploded! So 
there I was, on the plane of water, with no means of detecting the 
portal. I checked my inventory, but I had nothing. Finally, I put on the 
Amulet of Yendor, giving up reflection for a while, and started 
wandering around. I found the portal surprisingly quickly.

So I arrived on the astral plane, and was given an angel by the Lady. 
Death was on the left, Pestilence in the middle, and Famine on the 
right. Armed with my trusty wand of death (in the end I had recharged it 
5 times) I set out for the middle altar: chaotic. I wanted to heal up, 
but the door had been blown out, so I waded back to the beginning, and 
locked the door, since I had only about 150 hp (less than half) left. 
Monsters don't die quickly to a +4 Snickersnee and a +0 silver saber.

I went right next: neutral! Just before I stepped on the altar, I had a 
sad feeling for a moment, but as I offered the amulet, it passed.


